// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Delete Defender Scan ShellEx Context Menu Registry Key
// Sigma ID: 72a0369a-2576-4aaf-bfc9-6bb24a574ac6
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Matt Anderson (Huntress)
// Date: 2025-07-11 | Modified: 2025-10-07
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment
// Description: Detects deletion of registry key that adds 'Scan with Defender' option in context menu.
//   Attackers may use this to make it harder for users to scan files that are suspicious.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely as this weakens defenses and normally would not be done even if using another AV.
// References:
//   - https://research.splunk.com/endpoint/395ed5fe-ad13-4366-9405-a228427bdd91/
//   - https://winaero.com/how-to-delete-scan-with-windows-defender-from-context-menu-in-windows-10/
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2021/10/18/icedid-to-xinglocker-ransomware-in-24-hours/
//   - https://www.threatdown.com/blog/lazyscripter-from-empire-to-double-rat/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/windows/registry/registry_delete/registry_delete_defender_context_menu.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (ActionType in~ ("RegistryKeyDeleted", "RegistryValueDeleted")) and (RegistryKey contains "shellex\\ContextMenuHandlers\\EPP" and (not(((InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Platform\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\Windows Defender\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Windows Defender\\") and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\MsMpEng.exe"))))
